  "abstract_sentences": [
    {
      "index": 1,
      "text": "Direct alignment algorithms such as Direct Preference Optimization (DPO) fine-tune models based on preference data, using only supervised learning instead of two-stage reinforcement learning with human feedback (RLHF).",
      "word_count": 28,
      "functions": [
        "object_scope",
        "method"
      ],
      "evidence": {
        "page": 1,
        "section": "Abstract",
        "anchor": "using only supervised learning",
        "basis": "explicit"
      }
    },
    {
      "index": 2,
      "text": "We show that DPO encodes a statistical estimation problem over reward functions induced by a parametric policy class.",
      "word_count": 18,
      "functions": [
        "core_idea",
        "theory"
      ],
      "evidence": {
        "page": 1,
        "section": "Abstract",
        "anchor": "statistical estimation problem",
        "basis": "explicit"
      }
    },
    {
      "index": 3,
      "text": "When the true reward function that generates preferences cannot be realized via the policy class, DPO becomes misspecified, resulting in failure modes such as preference order reversal, worsening of policy reward, and high sensitivity to the input preference data distribution.",
      "word_count": 40,
      "functions": [
        "problem_gap",
        "theory"
      ],
      "evidence": {
        "page": 1,
        "section": "Abstract",
        "anchor": "cannot be realized",
        "basis": "explicit"
      }
    },
    {
      "index": 4,
      "text": "On the other hand, we study the local behavior of two-stage RLHF for a parametric class and relate it to a natural gradient step in policy space.",
      "word_count": 27,
      "functions": [
        "theory",
        "method"
      ],
      "evidence": {
        "page": 1,
        "section": "Abstract",
        "anchor": "natural gradient step",
        "basis": "explicit"
      }
    },
    {
      "index": 5,
      "text": "Our fine-grained geometric characterization allows us to propose AuxDPO, which introduces additional auxiliary variables in the DPO loss function to help move towards the RLHF solution in a principled manner and mitigate the misspecification in DPO.",
      "word_count": 36,
      "functions": [
        "core_idea",
        "method"
      ],
      "evidence": {
        "page": 1,
        "section": "Abstract",
        "anchor": "introduces additional auxiliary variables",
        "basis": "explicit"
      }
    },
    {
      "index": 6,
      "text": "We empirically demonstrate the superior performance of AuxDPO on didactic bandit settings as well as LLM alignment tasks.",
      "word_count": 18,
      "functions": [
        "experimental_setup",
        "qualitative_result"
      ],
      "evidence": {
        "page": 1,
        "section": "Abstract",
        "anchor": "superior performance of AuxDPO",
        "basis": "explicit"
      }
    }
  ],
